Below is what’s happening and the minimal fix you can apply:

1. In your scenario the sum of all your values (“max”) is over 7 million, so  
   (360 / max) × 10000  < 1 and `Math.floor(...)/10000` becomes `0`.  
2. That means every segment except the last ends up with zero angular extent, so only the final slice (which is forced to 360°) actually draws.  
3. The simplest fix is to stop over-truncating `anglePer`. You can either remove the truncation altogether or bump up the precision multiplier. Below we remove it.

```javascript
### src/js/components/Meter/Circle.js
